# Chapter 35: Pure Cryptography, Hashing & Wire Security

Cluster standard library provides pure, verified cryptographic algorithms implemented entirely in Cluster without linking to OpenSSL or external C libraries (`std/crypto.cl`):

## 1. Supported Cryptographic Primitives
- **RFC 3174 SHA-1**: 160-bit secure hashing algorithm.
- **FNV-1a & DJB2**: High-speed hash table hashing routines.
- **RFC 4648 Base64**: Constant-memory streaming encoder and decoder.

## 2. Example Usage

```cluster
import "std/crypto.cl"

fn main():
    data := "Cluster Secure Payload"
    hash := sha1(data)
    encoded := base64_encode(data)

    println("Payload SHA-1: " + hash)
    println("Base64:        " + encoded)
```
